[Music]  okay hi everyone and I'm glad to be in  the company of other language teachers  but the points that I'm going to talk  about and mention today don't really  have anything to do with campus with the  language so hopefully they'll be useful  to everyone so like many of you when we  first started using canvas I had this  huge fear of like oh my god this is  going to be a huge waste of time I'm  going to have to spend so much time  learning how to do this I'm going to  have to spend so much time putting all  my teaching resources on it this is a  new whole new learning process so what  I'm going to talk about today is like  things that I did in order to save time  and cut on time and things that I know  students appreciate it because not only  did it save me time but it saved them  time as well so I'm going to start from  the beginning and I'm sure you're  familiar with this picture this is what  we see when we first learn to log in to  canvas and you can see that we started  the tabs for the classes and the way to  tell one class from the other is the  color I don't know about you but about  as far as I'm concerned a number of  times I clicked on the wrong box and I  found myself in the wrong class and I'm  like no this is not at all what I want  to do and I have to go back a couple of  steps to enter an easy way to solve this  problem is if you personalize your class  and put a picture as to what each class  looks like so these are two of the  classes that I'm teaching this semester  each one has a picture it's a lot easier  for me to click on the right picture  when I want to go to the right class and  also as far as the students is concerned  because like you they have like four or  five tabs that are only different in  color but now when there's a picture to  your class they can easily identify and  access it quite easily another thing  that I found useful and saved me a lot  of time is using the calendar we've  heard already a couple of our presenters  mentioning different techniques of using  canvas calendar is one of them certainly  is not the only one  is where calendar is if you haven't used  it and when you click on it you can go  to the calendar and what you can do is  for every day or for every week or  multiple times a day you can set up  different events and what I do is I  start early before the beginning of the  semester I go to the calendar and I put  in every single test or quiz or a  writing assignment or grade of grading  activity or even activities that are not  graded that might be of importance to  the student and when you go to the  calendar when you click on each day this  is the tab that you're going to get what  allows you to put in either an activity  or an assignment and the details and the  link and the time etc etc the other  thing that you can do from the same  calendar is you can have it assigned to  two different classes or three different  classes for that matter as a language  teacher I teach multiple sections so  this is useful I don't have to do the  same thing again rather all I have to do  is change the class and add it to the  calendar of that class the other amazing  thing once I'm done on the main page of  what the students see they can see as  you can see right here all the times all  the activities that I've set up in the  calendar they're all there nicely  yeah arranged to chronologically so they  know when they have a test and when they  have quiz they don't need to ask me I  don't need the answer everybody's saving  time another nice thing about calendar  is that you can actually synchronize it  so if you click on this tab over here  you'll find out that there is an option  that you can add all these dates to your  Google Calendar whatever your personal  Google Calendar is you can add so this  is what you would get and if you take  the link and add it to your Google  Calendar all these dates will be added  to your Google Calendar so the students  can go that's especially helpful for the  students because they have other events  and other classes and other stuff that  they have to do this way they  see everything on their Google Calendar  without having to ask me and I don't  have to answer the other thing that I do  that saves me and the students time is I  use assignment and when I set up  assignments I give each one of them  value depending on category and when I  do that again through the magic of  canvas they can see on their first page  on the on the front page of the class  they can see exactly what are the graded  items that they have to go through and  how much each of them is worth yes we  have a syllabus in the syllabus we put  all this thing together but it's nice  for them through one-click as soon as  they sign in they can see all these  information without having to ask the  other advice that I have for everyone I  have been teaching for a while and I  have developed a number of teaching  resources and I found out using canvas  that there's always a way to embed  materials that you have had from the  past you don't need to do it again you  don't all you have to do is ask someone  or get the advice of someone and there's  always a way to embed your previous  materials I have successfully been able  to embed videos other teaching materials  that I've used in the past from other  technological resources and again I  teach elementary or at least I'm  teaching elementary this year so a lot  of my teaching material came from  different resources and I was successful  in embedding all of them and this  enables me to use it on the site for the  students as assignment or as homework  but even in the class it has been quite  useful and quite helpful and I didn't  have to change a whole lot of my  teaching materials so these were just  some tips from me that I hope that it  will save you some time and also save  your students some time which they will  appreciate thank you very much  [Applause]  and questions yes when you set up the  calendar do you have to do it every year  or you can't navigate it no no I'm  afraid you have to do it every semester  because the way I do it is depending on  the date that's why you can't move it  from one semester to the other it's yes  I set it up by the the dates that the  dates for the quizzes and the tests and  the written assignments if I set up the  calendar for my course from the student  perspective if they have a number of  different courses does their calendar  then show things from all the different  courses with different colors yes that's  exactly a complain that they can't  figure out what we how to sync their  lives up they have a way of doing that  if we've helped them by putting it on  the calendar yes exactly yes so whatever  items there are on the canvas calendar  they they will be different with  different colors and when you hover the  mouse over it it'll tell you the name of  the class like let's say they're not  sure what which class is the pink color  if you just hover the mouse over it it  will tell you which class that is canvas  tools do you use for to embed the  examples that you gave here for example  do you use assignments do you use the  quizzes  I've been able to embed stuff in assign  mostly assignments but also in the pages  and even on the front page I've been  able to embed stuff absolutely  calendar do is it possible for students  to like click on the event and have it  go directly to canvas yes yes absolutely  if it is something that will take that  is linked to an assignment or a quiz yes  it'll take them there right away  absolutely yep today because I use it  not only for my written quizzes if the  quiz is sellable in chronically you can  import in import from here to here and  the dates will adjust for you so it  automatically adjusts is beautiful you  don't have to do it by hand but presume  you don't want to put all your tests on  canvas so then it depends what you do if  you have say oral presentations  assignment then I believe again as long  as the date is given like today we hit  orals and the there is a tab submit  required submissions so that means when  I import resources for next year  the date will adjust for me in other  words it will still be that assignment  on Tuesday of whatever the new date it  will automatically adjust so yes you  will depends what type like the lights  fellow presentations obviously that you  have to input by hand but are the events  it will import so you don't have to do  all of it by hand  [Applause]  thank you  [Music]

